This file lists the third-party components carried by the `retsend` binary,
beyond the Rust standard library.

Rust crates (from the crate registry; licences as declared by each project)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

- sdl2 (sdl2-sys) — Rust SDL2 bindings; MIT OR Apache-2.0.
  Links the system SDL2 library at runtime, see below.
- egui-sdl2 — egui integration for SDL2, by the RetSend author
  (https://github.com/mxmgorin/egui-sdl2). Pulls in egui/epaint, eframe
  support crates, glow and bytemuck.
- egui, epaint, emath, ecolor, ab_glyph — the egui UI toolkit;
  MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- glow — OpenGL loader; MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- serde, serde_json, serde_derive — MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- toml, toml_edit, toml_writer — MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- log, env_logger — MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- ureq — HTTP client; MIT OR Apache-2.0. Pulls in (among others) rustls,
  webpki-roots, http, url, percent-encoding, base64, once_cell.
- rustls, rustls-pki-types, rustls-webpki, ring — TLS; rustls stack is
  MIT OR Apache-2.0 / ISC (ring). Uses the `ring` provider as configured.
- rcgen — self-signed certificate generation; MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- pem — PEM decoding; MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- sha2, digest, block-buffer, crypto-common — MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- getrandom — MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- socket2 — MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- libc — MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- png — PNG decoding (startup logo); MIT OR Apache-2.0. Pulls in crc32fast,
  flate2/miniz_oxide, fdeflate, bitflags.
- android_logger (Android builds only; not shipped in this package) —
  MIT OR Apache-2.0.

The complete dependency list with exact versions is recorded in Cargo.lock
in the source repository at the release tag. A per-crate licence inventory
(SBOM) is planned; where a crate above ships its own licence file, that file
is authoritative.

System libraries (not shipped; loaded from the device)
------------------------------------------------------

- libSDL2-2.0.so.0 — Simple DirectMedia Layer, zlib licence. Knulli supplies
  it; this package does not distribute it. RetSend requires SDL 2.0.18+
  (SDL_RenderGeometry).
- libc (glibc) — GNU C library, LGPL-2.1+. Provided by the device firmware.
- libm, libdl, libpthread — glibc components, as above.

Trademarks
----------

"LocalSend" is a project name of the LocalSend project; RetSend is not
affiliated with it, but implements its transfer protocol.
